SECTION      | KEY                | VALUE
----------------------------------------
META         | file_id            | keybinds
META         | note               | civ-snes book keybinds (2026-11-27, D157): the shape of rmmc's. While the rig:civ token is POSSESSED (In: ON, Enter on the piece) the engine does not move the cursor with the GAMEKEY keys: it appends `<code> <ms>` to the instance state/interact_relay.txt and civ_driver turns each into a verb page (keys.pdl names the verb). The camera keys y u i o p and l are the engine's and are not listed as GAMEKEY.
# GAMEKEY | name | keycode      arrows 1000 left, 1001 right, 1002 up, 1003 down (as rpg-pet and rmmc); space 32; raw X keysyms for Home 65360, PgUp 65365, PgDn 65366, End 65367, BackSpace 65288
GAMEKEY      | left | 1000
GAMEKEY      | right | 1001
